What the agent does:
I created an agent that answers technical questions asked by an user. User can can expect the agent to answer follow up questions as it will remember what was previously asked and said until the conversation is terminated.

Description of agent pipeline:
Document loader allows you to read data from different sources and into document that ensures that data is handled consistently. In our case, this is handled using WebBaseLoader. These documents are then cut to chunks to fit within model context window limit and be retreivable. Documents are vectorized or encoded through embedding to capture the semantic meaning of words and the machine is able to compare and search texts based on meaning rather than exact words. These embeded data are then stored in vector store and similiarity search is done to query for documents that are semantically similar to documents. Short term memory is saved to the agent in checkpointer which in our case is specified as using InMemorySaver.

Sources of documents fed:
I used documents from Oracle's Java documentation web page.

Failure noticed:
Agent may mistaken a question topic as being related to a document it is able to reference if the subject of a question is similar to a topic of a document it can reference in name (i.e. asking about hash tags may lead to the agent answering the question with topic of hashing instead and it will tell the user to not mistake it as the actual topic that was asked about).

To run, execute the file in order of document_loader, agent_cli.

